L0300: Independent checker rejected lowered code

The elaborator produced a candidate that the independent execution or proof checker rejected. Acceptance requires that second check. The detailed cause may identify a source restriction; if apparently valid source reaches this diagnostic, reduce it and report a compiler issue.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/checker_rejected.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```rust
// Proof-valued branches now check. A nested continue still reaches the
// independent checker rejection rather than being accepted.
fn choose(flag: bool) -> @(1 == 1) {
    if flag { _ } else { _ }
}

fn count(n: u8) -> u8 {
    let mut total: u8 = 0;
    for i in 0..n {
        let _ = continue;
        total = total.wrapping_add(i);
    }
    total
}
```

Language, as built: [1.23:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.23:1).
